@startuml
skinparam participantPadding 20
skinparam boxPadding 10

actor "User" as User
participant "App Logic\n(Repository)" as App
database "Local DB\n(SQLite/Drift)" as LocalDB
database "Cloud DB\n(Firestore)" as CloudDB

User -> App: Click **Sync Button**
activate App

note over App: START: Bidirectional Sync

== 1. Push Local Changes to Cloud ==

App -> LocalDB: Query items where **isSynced = false** AND **isDeleted = false**
LocalDB --> App: List<DirtyItems>

loop for each item in DirtyItems
    
    group Transaction / Atomic Operation
        App -> CloudDB: **UPSERT** item\n(set updatedAt = now())
        
        alt Cloud Write Success
            CloudDB --> App: Success
            App -> LocalDB: Update item\nset **isSynced = true**
        else Cloud Write Failed
            App -> App: Skip / Log Error\n(Keep isSynced = false to retry later)
        end
    end
    
end

note over App: DELETED ITEMS: Push soft deletes

App -> LocalDB: Query items where **isDeleted = true**
LocalDB --> App: List<DeletedItems>

loop for each deleted item
    App -> CloudDB: Update item\nset **isDeleted = true, updatedAt = now()**
end

note over App: PUSH COMPLETED. START: Pull from Cloud

== 2. Pull Changes from Cloud ==

App -> CloudDB: Query items\n(all categories for this user)
CloudDB --> App: List<CloudCategories>

loop for each item in CloudCategories
    
    note right of App
        Merge Logic:
        Cloud data has priority
        (Cloud as Source of Truth)
    end note

    alt item.isDeleted == true
        App -> LocalDB: **Soft Delete**\nset isDeleted = true\nset isSynced = true
    else item.isDeleted == false
        alt item exists locally
            App -> LocalDB: **UPDATE** with cloud data\nset isSynced = true
        else item is new
            App -> LocalDB: **INSERT** from cloud\nset isSynced = true
        end
    end
    
end

note over App: SYNC COMPLETED

App --> User: Show "Sync Completed"
deactivate App

@enduml